{%- comment -%}
  PG Gift Guard: owns the free case. It now RIDES ALONG with the console's own
  add-to-cart instead of chasing it, and it no longer fights pg-case-mobile
  over the gift line.

  ================================================================
  1. THE GIFT ARRIVES WITH THE CONSOLE, IN ONE REQUEST   (2026-09-12)

  Reported: "whenever I add an R36 to cart it takes a minute to load in the
  free gift." It did, and the shape of this file was the reason.

  Placement used to hang off the POLL below. The whole chain, measured:

      tap ADD TO CART   ->  POST /cart/add.js            (console lands)
      drawer opens                                        (console only)
      up to 2000ms      ->  the next check() tick
                        ->  GET /cart.js                  (is a gift needed?)
                        ->  GET /cart.js again            ("one more read")
                        ->  POST /cart/add.js             (the gift)
                        ->  pgDrawerRefresh()             (>=700ms floor in
                                                           pg-cart-fast, then a
                                                           full GET of `/`)
      drawer's innerHTML is REPLACED                      (console + gift)

  So the gift could not appear in under about a second and a half even on a
  fast connection, and on a phone whose /cart.js reads were being throttled it
  was far worse -- the note further down records a console sitting for 15s with
  no case. Worse than the wait: that last step replaces the drawer's markup
  wholesale, so every stamping script on the page (pg-case-mobile, nc-linesave,
  pg-chips, pg-drawer) re-runs against brand new nodes while the shopper is
  looking at them. A second cart mutation a beat after the first IS the
  re-render the shopper sees as the cart "glitching".

  THE FIX IS TO NOT MAKE A SECOND REQUEST. window.fetch is wrapped, and a POST
  to /cart/add.js carrying a console, Duo Pack or Trio Pack variant gets the
  free case appended to ITS OWN items array. One round trip, and the server's
  answer already contains both lines -- so the drawer's first paint has the
  gift in it, there is no follow-up write, and there is no second render.

  The wrapper is deliberately narrow. It rewrites nothing unless:
    - the method is POST and the URL is /cart/add.js,
    - the body is a string of JSON (every add path in this theme posts that),
    - an item in it is a known gift-earning variant,
    - and this file KNOWS the cart has no gift yet (giftIn === false).
  Anything else is passed through untouched. It composes with pg-cart-fast's
  wrapper, which is installed later (footer-group) and therefore calls this
  one; its cache invalidation still sees the same URL and still fires.

  The earning variant ids are seeded below AND re-learned from the products
  themselves on load, so a new console or pack variant cannot silently stop
  earning a case.

  THE POLL STAYS, as the safety net it should always have been: an add made by
  a path the wrapper does not see (a form POST, a Shopify quick-add) still gets
  its gift within a tick, and every write now nudges a check 250ms later rather
  than waiting out the full 2s interval.

  ================================================================
  2. THE 250ms TUG-OF-WAR OVER data-pg-free   (2026-09-12)

  Reported: "the free gift text and the $0 price glitch up and down
  repeatedly." Two intervals were writing and deleting one attribute on the
  same line, four times a second.

      pg-case-mobile asGift()   every 250ms:  li.dataset.pgFree = '1'
      pg-giftguard   apply()    every 250ms:  delete li.dataset.pgFree

  apply()'s release clause read "marked as handled but wearing no badge, so
  release it" -- and it looked for .pg-free-tag. pg-case-mobile deliberately
  stopped using that class (it benches it and renders .pg-truegift-tag instead,
  "one writer, no race"), so the clause matched the gift line on EVERY pass and
  deleted an attribute pg-case-mobile put back a quarter-second later, forever.

  That attribute is not cosmetic. pg-drawer styles the whole gift module from
  it:

      li[data-pg-free] > section > p      display:none   (the variant text)
      li[data-pg-free] > section          grid-template-rows changes
      li[data-pg-free] figure img         height:110px, width:auto

  So the thumbnail resized, the variant line appeared and vanished, and the row
  grew and shrank -- dragging the pill and the $0.00 with it. That is the
  up-and-down, and it is why it looked worst on the free case specifically.

  Two changes end it:

    - the release clause counts .pg-truegift-tag as a badge, so a line
      pg-case-mobile has stamped is left alone;
    - the unearned branch no longer WRITES data-pg-free at all. It only ever
      set it as a private "handled" marker, but the attribute is pg-drawer's
      layout switch, so stamping it on a paid spare case turned that row into a
      gift module and put pg-case-mobile's asPaid() (which deletes it, every
      250ms) into the same fight. Ownership of the attribute is pg-case-mobile's
      alone now; this file reads it and never writes it.

  ================================================================
  background (unchanged)

  The case product carries two real variants:

      49640846426340  $0.00   "Free with console"   -> the gift
      49640879063268  $13.99  "Spare case"          -> the paid upsell

  The gift is free because it is priced at zero, which leaves Shopify's single
  automatic-discount slot free for the bundle ladders.

  ONE GIFT, NEVER TWO. Detection is BY VARIANT, never by a property: a line can
  be rebuilt, merged or re-added by another section and lose the marker while
  still being the free case sitting in the cart. An add is followed by a
  cooldown and re-checked against a fresh read. The gift line is capped at one
  unit by REMOVAL -- pg-drawer and pg-case-mobile both answer a surplus by
  selling it as a $13.99 spare, and taking it off first leaves them nothing to
  sell. A unit that arrived by accident is not an upsell.
{%- endcomment -%}
<script>
(function(){
  if (window.pgGiftGuard) return; window.pgGiftGuard = 1;

  var CASE_LINK = 'free-gift';               /* the case handle ends in -free-gift */
  var CONSOLE_HANDLE = 'handheld-game-console';
  /* The Duo and Trio Packs are their own products, so a cart holding one
     contains no console line at all. Either handle earns the gift. */
  var DUO_HANDLE = 'r36s-duo-pack';
  var TRIO_HANDLE = 'r36s-trio-pack';
  function earnsGift(it){
    return it.handle === CONSOLE_HANDLE || it.handle === DUO_HANDLE || it.handle === TRIO_HANDLE;
  }
  var FREE_VARIANT = 49640846426340;         /* $0.00 "Free with console" */
  var LINES = '#cart .l4ca > li, body.template-cart .form-cart .l4ca > li';
  /* null = not checked yet. The badge is only ever removed on an explicit
     false, so a failed or pending /cart.js never blanks a legitimate gift. */
  var earned = null;
  var busy = false;
  var adding = false;
  /* No add may follow another inside this window, however many reads come back
     saying the cart is empty of gifts. 8s comfortably outlasts a throttled
     response and every drawer refresh it can trigger. */
  var COOLDOWN = 8000;
  var lastAdd = 0;
  var capping = false;

  /* ============================================================
     THE RIDE-ALONG: the gift goes in the console's own add request
     ============================================================ */

  /* Seeded, then re-learned from the products below. A hardcoded list alone
     would quietly stop earning the gift the day a variant is added. */
  var EARNING_VARIANTS = {
    49622431858916: 1, 49622431826148: 1,                                       /* R36S 64G / 128G */
    49831383531748: 1, 49831383564516: 1, 49831383597284: 1, 49831405846756: 1, /* Duo Pack */
    49835591270628: 1, 49835591565540: 1, 49835591598308: 1, 49835591631076: 1  /* Trio Pack */
  };
  /* null = unknown. The wrapper only ever injects on an explicit false, so a
     page whose first cart read has not landed yet simply falls back to the
     poll rather than risking a second gift. */
  var giftIn = null;

  function learnVariants(){
    [CONSOLE_HANDLE, DUO_HANDLE, TRIO_HANDLE].forEach(function(h){
      fetch('/products/' + h + '.js', {headers: {'Accept': 'application/json'}})
        .then(function(r){ return r.ok ? r.json() : null; })
        .then(function(p){
          if (p && p.variants) p.variants.forEach(function(v){ EARNING_VARIANTS[v.id] = 1; });
        })
        .catch(function(){});
    });
  }

  /* Returns a rewritten body, or null to leave the request alone. */
  function withGift(bodyStr){
    if (giftIn !== false) return null;
    if (Date.now() - lastAdd < 1500) return null;   /* one already in flight */
    var b;
    try { b = JSON.parse(bodyStr); } catch (e){ return null; }
    if (!b || typeof b !== 'object') return null;
    var items = Array.isArray(b.items) ? b.items : (b.id ? [b] : null);
    if (!items || !items.length) return null;
    var earns = false, already = false;
    items.forEach(function(it){
      var id = parseInt(it && it.id, 10);
      if (EARNING_VARIANTS[id]) earns = true;
      if (id === FREE_VARIANT) already = true;
    });
    if (!earns || already) return null;
    /* keep every other top-level key the caller sent (sections, form_type,
       attributes); only the item list is replaced */
    var out = {};
    for (var k in b){
      if (k === 'id' || k === 'quantity' || k === 'properties' || k === 'items') continue;
      out[k] = b[k];
    }
    out.items = items.concat([{id: FREE_VARIANT, quantity: 1, properties: {_free_gift: 'yes'}}]);
    giftIn = true;          /* the request on its way carries it */
    lastAdd = Date.now();   /* and the fallback add must not race it */
    return JSON.stringify(out);
  }

  var soonTimer = null, soonTimer2 = null;
  function soon(){
    clearTimeout(soonTimer); clearTimeout(soonTimer2);
    soonTimer = setTimeout(check, 250);
    soonTimer2 = setTimeout(check, 1200);
  }

  function wrapFetch(){
    var next = window.fetch;
    if (typeof next !== 'function') return;
    window.fetch = function(input, init){
      var url = typeof input === 'string' ? input
              : (input && typeof input.url === 'string' ? input.url : '');
      var method = String((init && init.method) || (input && input.method) || 'GET').toUpperCase();
      var isWrite = method === 'POST' && /\/cart\/(add|change|update|clear)(\.js)?(\?|$)/.test(url);

      if (method === 'POST' && /\/cart\/add(\.js)?(\?|$)/.test(url) &&
          typeof input === 'string' && init && typeof init.body === 'string'){
        var body = withGift(init.body);
        if (body){
          var ni = {};
          for (var k in init) ni[k] = init[k];
          ni.body = body;
          var pr = next.call(this, input, ni);
          /* a rejected or failed add did NOT place the gift: forget the
             optimistic flag so the poll can put one in */
          if (pr && typeof pr.then === 'function'){
            pr.then(function(r){ if (!r || !r.ok) giftIn = null; }, function(){ giftIn = null; });
          }
          soon();
          return pr;
        }
      }

      var p = next.apply(this, arguments);
      if (isWrite) soon();
      return p;
    };
  }

  /* ============================================================
     the badge
     ============================================================ */

  function caseLines(){
    var out = [];
    document.querySelectorAll(LINES).forEach(function(li){
      if (li.querySelector('a[href*="' + CASE_LINK + '"]')) out.push(li);
    });
    return out;
  }

  /* READS data-pg-free, NEVER WRITES IT -- see note 2 at the top. Its owner is
     pg-case-mobile, which sets it on the $0.00 line and clears it on the paid
     one, by variant, every 250ms. */
  function apply(){
    var lis = caseLines();
    if (!lis.length) return;
    if (earned === false){
      /* the legacy pill only: .pg-truegift-tag belongs to pg-case-mobile,
         which already takes it off the paid line by variant, and removing it
         here would be the same fight in a different costume */
      lis.forEach(function(li){
        li.querySelectorAll('.pg-free-tag').forEach(function(el){
          if (el.parentNode) el.parentNode.removeChild(el);
        });
      });
    }
  }

  /* The gift line, BY VARIANT. */
  function giftLine(cart){
    var found = null;
    (cart.items || []).forEach(function(it){
      if (it.variant_id === FREE_VARIANT) found = it;
    });
    return found;
  }

  /* THE FALLBACK PLACEMENT. The ride-along above is the normal path; this
     covers an add this page never saw. Guarded three ways -- an in-flight add,
     a cooldown, and a fresh read taken at the moment of the decision. */
  function ensureGift(cart){
    if (adding) return;
    if (Date.now() - lastAdd < COOLDOWN) return;
    var items = cart.items || [];
    if (!items.some(earnsGift)) return;
    if (giftLine(cart)) return;
    adding = true;
    fetch('/cart.js', {headers: {'X-Requested-With': 'XMLHttpRequest'}})
      .then(function(r){ return r.json(); })
      .then(function(fresh){
        if (giftLine(fresh) || !(fresh.items || []).some(earnsGift)){
          adding = false;
          return;
        }
        lastAdd = Date.now();
        return fetch('/cart/add.js', {
          method: 'POST', headers: {'Content-Type': 'application/json'},
          body: JSON.stringify({items: [{id: FREE_VARIANT, quantity: 1, properties: {_free_gift: 'yes'}}]})
        }).then(function(r){
          adding = false;
          if (!r.ok) return;
          giftIn = true;
          if (window.pgDrawerRefresh) return window.pgDrawerRefresh();
        });
      })
      .catch(function(){ adding = false; });
  }

  /* One free case, never more. Removal only, and only ever of the $0.00
     variant -- a spare the shopper actually chose is a different variant and
     is never touched. */
  function capGift(cart){
    if (capping || adding) return;
    var gift = giftLine(cart);
    if (!gift || gift.quantity <= 1) return;
    capping = true;
    fetch('/cart/change.js', {
      method: 'POST', headers: {'Content-Type': 'application/json'},
      credentials: 'same-origin',
      body: JSON.stringify({id: gift.key, quantity: 1})
    }).then(function(){
      capping = false;
      if (window.pgDrawerRefresh) return window.pgDrawerRefresh();
    }).catch(function(){ capping = false; });
  }

  /* WITH A WATCHDOG: one stuck flag must never disable the gift for the rest
     of a session. */
  var busyTimer = null;
  function check(){
    if (busy) return;
    busy = true;
    clearTimeout(busyTimer);
    busyTimer = setTimeout(function(){ busy = false; }, 8000);
    fetch('/cart.js', {headers: {'X-Requested-With': 'XMLHttpRequest'}})
      .then(function(r){ return r.json(); })
      .then(function(c){
        /* the flag the wrapper reads. It is only ever lowered by a read taken
           well clear of an add: a cached answer issued before an injected add
           landed must not be allowed to license a second gift. */
        if (giftLine(c)) giftIn = true;
        else if (Date.now() - lastAdd > 1500) giftIn = false;
        earned = (c.items || []).some(function(it){
          return earnsGift(it) || (it.properties && it.properties._free_gift);
        });
        clearTimeout(busyTimer); busy = false;
        apply();
        capGift(c);
        ensureGift(c);
      })
      .catch(function(){ clearTimeout(busyTimer); busy = false; });
  }

  wrapFetch();
  learnVariants();
  /* apply() is cheap and runs often so a stale badge never lingers between
     cart reads; check() re-reads on a slower beat, because /cart.js is shared
     with five other sections (pg-cart-fast memoises it for them all). */
  setInterval(apply, 250);
  setInterval(check, 2000);
  check();
})();
</script>
{% schema %}
{"name": "PG Gift Guard", "settings": []}
{% endschema %}
